    "https://www.ccis.edu/careers/jobs?gnk=job&gni=8a7885aca0abfc6901a0caf9d36f6b3b&lang=en": {
      "title": "Professional Tutor",
      "description": "Professional Tutor.  Professional Tutor Department: Stafford Library Location: Hybrid Type: Part-time; Staff Pay: $15.00 per hour Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; visa sponsorship is not available for this position Job Summary: The Professional Tutor provides individualized and small-group academic support to Columbia College students in STEM disciplines and/or writing. This position helps students strengthen subject knowledge, develop effective academic strategies, and build confidence as independent learners. Working collaboratively with Learning Commons staff and faculty, the Professional Tutor provides accessible, student-centered academic assistance in their designated areas of expertise while maintaining a welcoming and inclusive learning environment. Essential Functions: Academic Tutoring and Student Support Provide individual and small-group tutoring in assigned STEM disciplines and/or writing. Assess student learning needs and adapt tutoring approaches to support individual learning styles and academic goals. Explain complex concepts clearly while encouraging critical thinking, problem-solving, and independent learning. Assist students in developing effective study habits, time management strategies, and academic confidence. Support students in understanding course expectations, preparing for examinations, and applying academic concepts. Maintain academic integrity by guiding students through coursework without completing assignments on their behalf. Discipline-Specific Tutoring depending on qualifications and assigned responsibilities Provide STEM tutoring in mathematics, science, and related disciplines, emphasizing conceptual understanding and problem-solving strategies. Support students throughout the writing process, including brainstorming, organization, thesis development, revision, and editing strategies. Assist students with academic writing conventions, citation practices, and appropriate use of research materials. Help students develop transferable skills that support success across courses and academic disciplines. Collaboration and Student Engagement Collaborate with faculty and Learning Commons staff to identify student learning needs and provide appropriate academic support. Refer students to additional tutoring services, library resources, faculty, or campus support services as appropriate. Foster a welcoming, inclusive, and supportive learning environment for students from diverse academic backgrounds. Promote student engagement with Learning Commons academic support services. Administrative and Professional Responsibilities: Maintain accurate tutoring records and appointment documentation using designated scheduling software. Communicate professionally and promptly with students and staff regarding appointments, scheduling, and academic support needs. Participate in required tutor training, meetings, and professional development. Maintain student confidentiality in accordance with FERPA and institutional policies. Follow established Learning Commons procedures and Columbia College policies. Assist with academic support initiatives and other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Associate degree or equivalent college coursework in a STEM discipline, English, writing, education, or a closely related field. Demonstrated proficiency in at least one designated tutoring area: STEM or writing. Strong communication, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills. Ability to explain academic concepts clearly and adapt instruction to individual student needs. Demonstrated professionalism, reliability, and commitment to student success. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an academic environment. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher in a relevant academic discipline. Previous experience in tutoring, teaching, academic support, or related instruction. Experience supporting college students, adult learners, or students from diverse academic backgrounds. Experience providing academic writing assistance or tutoring in mathematics and science. Familiarity with learning strategies and instructional approaches that support diverse learners. Experience with online tutoring platforms and academic scheduling software. Working Conditions: Work is performed in the Stafford Learning Commons, designated campus tutoring locations, or virtually as assigned. Scheduling is based on student demand and institutional needs and may include evening hours. Physical Requirements: Ability to perform essential job duties in an academic environment, including using computers and instructional technology and communicating with students in person or virtually, with or without reasonable accommodation. Physical Requirements: The physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Individuals seeking accommodation should contact the Human Resources Department without delay. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit for long periods of time, talk, and hear. The employee is required to use hands and fingers to handle or feel; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, or crawl. Employee must be able to type on a computer keyboard and use a computer monitor on a regular basis. Work Conditions: The work environment conditions described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is rarely exposed to outside weather conditions; however, possible exposure to hazards and physical risks to personal safety may occur while operating certain equipment. The noise level in the work environment is usually mild. This position is designated by the institution as a “Campus Security Authority” (CSA). As a CSA, you are required to report any information you receive about crimes occurring on or near campus to the Director of Campus Safety. This job description is not meant to be all-inclusive of every duty and responsibility required by the employee in the position. Eligibility for employee benefits and perks is determined by employment status. For more information please see https://www.ccis.edu/careers. The offer of employment and assignment to duties is contingent upon a satisfactory criminal background check. The information may include, but is not limited to, academic, residential, achievement, performance, attendance, disciplinary, employment history, credit history, driving history, and criminal history of public record. Columbia College is committed to creating an inclusive employee experience for all regardless of race, color, national origin, gender, religion, sexual orientation, age or disability. The college maintains a safe place for open discourse and overall, fosters a sense of community that welcomes everyone. In compliance with the Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) and the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), the Department of Campus Safety for Columbia College has provided the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report and crime statistics for the main campus and venues nationwide. Columbia College is required to distribute this information to all current and prospective employees and students. Please follow the link below for the full report or contact Human Resources at 573-875-7495 for a printed copy. http://www.ccis.edu/offices/campussafety/reportsandstats.aspx Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.ccis.edu/careers/jobs?gnk=job&gni=8a7883aca03fc27d01a0447e68fa3ba7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Peer Tutor Department: Stafford Library Rate of Pay: $15 Per Hour",
      "description": "Peer Tutor Department: Stafford Library Rate of Pay: $15 Per Hour.  Student Position: Peer Tutor Department: Stafford Library Rate of Pay: $15 Per Hour Location: Columbia College Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States\" visa sponsorship in not available for this position. Job Summary: The Peer Tutor provides academic support to Columbia College students in STEM and Writing disciplines through individual and small-group tutoring sessions. Working as a member of the Stafford Learning Commons, Peer Tutors help students strengthen course content knowledge, develop effective study strategies, build research skills, practice academic writing, and build confidence as independent learners. Peer Tutors create a welcoming, supportive, and inclusive learning environment while maintaining professionalism, confidentiality, and high standards of academic integrity. Tutors receive ongoing training and are expected to participate in professional development consistent with College and CRLA tutoring best practices. Essential Functions: Provide one-on-one and small-group tutoring in approved subject areas. These include, but are not limited to: Mathematics Biology Chemistry Computer Science Business (Finance, Accounting, etc.) Nursing All Writing Subjects Assist students in understanding course concepts while encouraging independent learning and critical thinking. Help students develop effective study habits, problem-solving skills, and learning strategies. Encourage student confidence and academic persistence through positive and supportive interactions. Maintain appropriate professional boundaries by guiding students without completing coursework for them. Attend all scheduled tutoring appointments, shifts, meetings, and required training sessions. Maintain accurate tutoring records and appointment documentation using designated software. Communicate professionally and promptly with Learning Commons staff regarding scheduling or availability. Maintain confidentiality of student information in accordance with institutional policies and FERPA. Foster a welcoming and inclusive environment for students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles. Refer students to additional Learning Commons services, library resources, faculty, or campus support services when appropriate. Promote the use of tutoring services through positive engagement with students. Supervisory Responsibility: No Position Reports to: Director of Library Services and Educational Resources Required Core Competencies and Profession Experience: Assist with Learning Commons events, outreach activities, and student engagement initiatives as assigned Participate in ongoing tutor training and professional development. Perform other related duties as assigned. Foster a respectful, professional, and student-centered environment in all interactions. Attend work reliably and on time during scheduled hours; work additional hours as needed. Practice superior customer service. Fulfill additional responsibilities as assigned. Qualifications: Current Columbia College student in good academic standing, Completion of the course(s) to be tutored with a grade of A or B (or department approval), Minimum cumulative GPA of 3.0 (preferred within coursework), Strong interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills, demonstrated reliability, professionalism, and dependability, Ability to explain technical concepts clearly and patiently, Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with Learning Commons staff. Preferred Core Competencies and Professional Experience: Previous tutoring, mentoring, teaching, supplemental instruction, or peer leadership experience. Strong interest in helping fellow students succeed academically. Willingness to complete CRLA tutor training and participate in ongoing professional development. Experience working with students from diverse backgrounds. Required Level of Education: High School Other Requirements: Ability to satisfy, within the parameters set by the College and consistent with applicable federal, state and local laws, a criminal background check as a condition of employment. Special Requirements (if any): Ability to work both mornings and evenings as needed when classes are in session (7:30am – 8pm). Physical Requirements: The physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Individuals seeking accommodation should contact the Human Resources Department without delay. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit for long periods of time, talk, and hear. The employee is required to use hands and fingers to handle or feel; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, or crawl. Employee must be able to type on a computer keyboard and use a computer monitor on a regular basis. Work Conditions: The work environment conditions described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is rarely exposed to outside weather conditions; however, possible exposure to hazards and physical risks to personal safety may occur while operating certain equipment. The noise level in the work environment is usually mild. This job description is not meant to be all-inclusive of every duty and responsibility required by the employee in the position. The offer of employment and assignment to duties is contingent upon a satisfactory criminal background check. The information may include, but is not limited to, academic, residential, achievement, performance, attendance, disciplinary, employment history, credit history, driving history, and criminal history of public record. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Columbia College is an equal opportunity employer. Columbia College is committed to creating an inclusive employee experience for all regardless of race, color, national origin, gender, religion, sexual orientation, age or disability. The college maintains a safe place for open discourse and overall, fosters a sense of community that welcomes everyone. In compliance with the Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) and the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), the Department of Campus Safety for Columbia College has provided the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report and crime statistics for the main campus and venues nationwide. Columbia College is required to distribute this information to all current and prospective employees and students. Please follow the link below for the full report or contact Human Resources at 573-875-7495 for a printed copy. https://www.ccis.edu/campus-safety/crime-reporting/reports-stats Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.ccis.edu/careers/jobs?gnk=job&gni=8a7885a86cf02eb8016cf8075a920ca5&lang=en": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor.  Adjunct Instructor Department: Columbia College Global Location: Denver, CO Type: Academic, Part-time Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Job Summary: Columbia College-Denver seeks an Adjunct (part-time) instructor to teach in-seat Mathematics, World History, World History, American History, Speech Communications, Computer Information Systems, Business Administration, and Science courses. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include a Master's Degree in the related field including courses directly related to content area. Current workplace experience in an associated field and college teaching experience are highly desired. Physical Requirements: The physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Individuals seeking accommodation should contact the Human Resources Department without delay. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit for long periods of time, talk, and hear. The employee is required to use hands and fingers to handle or feel; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, or crawl. Employee must be able to type on a computer keyboard and use a computer monitor on a regular basis. Work Conditions: The work environment conditions described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is rarely exposed to outside weather conditions; however, possible exposure to hazards and physical risks to personal safety may occur while operating certain equipment. The noise level in the work environment is usually mild. This position is designated by the institution as a “Campus Security Authority” (CSA). As a CSA, you are required to report any information you receive about crimes occurring on or near campus to the Director of Campus Safety. This job description is not meant to be all-inclusive of every duty and responsibility required by the employee in the position. Eligibility for employee benefits and perks is determined by employment status. For more information please see https://www.ccis.edu/careers. The offer of employment and assignment to duties is contingent upon a satisfactory criminal background check. The information may include, but is not limited to, academic, residential, achievement, performance, attendance, disciplinary, employment history, credit history, driving history, and criminal history of public record. Columbia College is committed to creating an inclusive employee experience for all regardless of race, color, national origin, gender, religion, sexual orientation, age or disability. The college maintains a safe place for open discourse and overall, fosters a sense of community that welcomes everyone. In compliance with the Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) and the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), the Department of Campus Safety for Columbia College has provided the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report and crime statistics for the main campus and venues nationwide. Columbia College is required to distribute this information to all current and prospective employees and students. Please follow the link below for the full report or contact Human Resources at 573-875-7495 for a printed copy. http://www.ccis.edu/offices/campussafety/reportsandstats.aspx Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.ccis.edu/careers/jobs?gnk=job&gni=8a7885a8798f6ffd0179d2ca915d79eb&lang=en": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Instructor Pool.  Online Adjunct Instructor (Pool) Department: Online Education Location: Online (Remote) Type: Academic, Part-time Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Description: Columbia College Online Education is accepting applications for adjunct (part-time) instructors to meet our changing needs. After completing the application process, the candidate's application will be considered active for two years. Qualified applicants will be contacted if an opening in their respective fields becomes available. After two years, candidates may reapply to update their application and restate their interest. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications to teach undergraduate courses include a master’s degree in the related field including courses directly related to content area. Minimum qualifications to teach graduate courses include a doctorate degree in the related field including courses directly related to content area. Current professional experience in an associated field and higher education teaching experience are highly desired. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Required Application Materials: Current resume or curriculum vitae Unofficial graduate transcripts Official graduate transcripts will be required upon offer of employment. The offer of employment and assignment to duties is contingent upon successful completion of our new instructor training course. Physical Requirements: The physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Individuals seeking accommodation should contact the Human Resources Department without delay. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit for long periods of time, talk, and hear. The employee is required to use hands and fingers to handle or feel; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, or crawl. Employee must be able to type on a computer keyboard and use a computer monitor on a regular basis. Work Conditions: The work environment conditions described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is rarely exposed to outside weather conditions; however, possible exposure to hazards and physical risks to personal safety may occur while operating certain equipment. The noise level in the work environment is usually mild. This position is designated by the institution as a “Campus Security Authority” (CSA). As a CSA, you are required to report any information you receive about crimes occurring on or near campus to the Director of Campus Safety. This job description is not meant to be all-inclusive of every duty and responsibility required by the employee in the position. Eligibility for employee benefits and perks is determined by employment status. For more information please see https://www.ccis.edu/careers. The offer of employment and assignment to duties is contingent upon a satisfactory criminal background check. The information may include, but is not limited to, academic, residential, achievement, performance, attendance, disciplinary, employment history, credit history, driving history, and criminal history of public record. Columbia College is committed to creating an inclusive employee experience for all regardless of race, color, national origin, gender, religion, sexual orientation, age or disability. The college maintains a safe place for open discourse and overall, fosters a sense of community that welcomes everyone. In compliance with the Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) and the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), the Department of Campus Safety for Columbia College has provided the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report and crime statistics for the main campus and venues nationwide. Columbia College is required to distribute this information to all current and prospective employees and students. Please follow the link below for the full report or contact Human Resources at 573-875-7495 for a printed copy. http://www.ccis.edu/offices/campussafety/reportsandstats.aspx Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
